# Plugin constants the rendering tests pin, loaded last so it wins over what the
# extension ships.
#
# The extension defaults to grouping a profile list by the first letter of the last name.
# The tests below this file are about ordering, localization and pagination, and their
# templates render a different markup for a grouped list, so they turn grouping off and
# assert the flat list. A test that is about grouping sets the constant itself.
plugin.tx_academicpersons.demand.groupBy =

# The extension defaults to sorting by last name. Before the defaults of the two
# delivery mechanisms were reconciled, the shipped value was empty in
# "constants.typoscript" and "title" in the site sets, and "title" is a value
# "demand.allowedSortByValues" does not accept, so
# "ProfileRepository::getOrderingsFromDemand()" discarded it - these tests were written
# against that unordered result. They are about localization, not ordering, so they keep
# asserting it. A test that is about ordering sets the constant itself.
plugin.tx_academicpersons.demand.sortBy =
